    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d332-a1">

                <pb facs="0275" n="201" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg201"/>

                <head>Mr. Pennington to Mr. Drouyn de Lhuys.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-12-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 2, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Monsieur le Ministre:</hi> I have to communicate to
                    your excellency the painful intelligence of the death of the Hon. William L.
                    Dayton, envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of the United States in
                    France. This event occurred last evening at nine o’clock, after an illness of a
                    few minutes.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to present to your excellency assurances of my high
                    consideration.</p>
                <p>Your obedient servant, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM S. PENNINGTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>M. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Drouyn de Lhuys,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Minister of Foreign Affairs, Paris.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
